+<div class="band"><div class="wrap">
+  <h1>AcquireIQ on AWS</h1>
+  <p class="lede">How the app runs once <code>infra/main.tf</code> and <code>infra/bootstrap/main.tf</code> are applied: one HTTPS address in front, a private database behind, and a GitHub Actions workflow that builds and ships every release.</p>
+  <span class="status">Design from the Terraform files. Not yet deployed or tested against AWS.</span>
+  <div class="warn"><strong>Two major deficiencies, accepted for this demo</strong><ol><li><b>No API authentication.</b> Anyone with the URL can read, create and change acquisition requests and record approvals.</li><li><b>No rate limiting.</b> Anyone can flood the API, including the search endpoint that calls OpenAI. Set a monthly spending limit on the OpenAI key.</li></ol>Both must be added before this holds real data. Details are in the last section.</div>
